A||||21||PAUL88GT||LeBra or Wolf. Which is better?||||5||
Z||000000||PAUL88GT||05-24-2000||02:49 PM||||Which of these car bras look better on an 88GT? I have to have one because the bugs are thick in my area. My research shows the following costs:<P>LeBra: $65 at Autozone<BR>Wolf: $70 at Fierostore<P>TIA<BR>Paul||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||05-24-2000||02:58 PM||||I've had both in the past (both on a 89 camaro) and hands down i would have to say LeBra is deffinately better. It holds its elactisity, shape, and last alot longer then wolf bras.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||05-24-2000||03:22 PM||||will they order them for the GT's?  my paint is really really bad on the front and i would like to have one.  yet I have never seen one on the shelf... arent to many Fiero Gt's these days.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||05-24-2000||04:12 PM||||I bought a Colgan bra through the dealership for about 80.00 bucks.  I've had it over a year and it's still looking brand new and has a good fit.  It covers the hood past the headlights and all the fender in front of the wheel well.  The only thing I don't like is that it makes it a process to get into the front hood.  I have to unhook four hook and scooch it down a little to get in the hood.  The sunroof has to come off on sunny days <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Road trip to Lake Nacimiento this weekend too.  Yahoooo!  Bikiniville!||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||05-24-2000||04:18 PM||||Oh yeah, the headlight covers are hook and loop.  Those have to be rolled up manually before turning on your headlights.  I tend to leave them rolled up tight if I think I'm doing more night driving than day.  I like the look better with them unrolled.  By the way I have an 86GT.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JAMIE||05-24-2000||04:28 PM||||I have had both a LeBra and a Colgan.I like the look of the Colgan much better and found it to be more durable than the LeBra.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fret Naught||05-24-2000||05:52 PM||||I purchased a wolf from the fiero store about six weeks ago, to be honest, it looks better than the chipped paint, but because of the fender liners and front design, I had to modify the install a bit. It does not fit as tight as I would like, and because I needed a liscense plate braket (the bra did not come with a pouch for one) it sticks out a bit and looks kind of tacky. When I get around to painting it, I am going to lose the Bra.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fret Naught||05-24-2000||05:57 PM||||Just remembered, if you do a thread search I have a couple of pics posted On 5/5/2000, the topic is "How is this" if you look close, you will see what I am talking about.||||reg||4
Z||000008||terryk||05-24-2000||08:49 PM||||FYI, I've had Perfect Fit's fall apart (stitching). Wolfs seem to hold up well. Never seen a LeBra.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierodave||05-26-2000||01:07 AM||||LeBra! <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=101570&a=1074965&p=19994891&Sequence=5" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=101570&a=1074965&p=19994891&Sequence=5</A> ||||reg||14
