Z||000011||tgowens||05-26-2000||10:44 AM||||I bought a Wolf because of a couple of trips I had to take back east -- one thing I like about it is that it covers the complete front (even covers the parking lights with clear plastic) and seems to be made well - it is a tricky fit on the '87 GT and yes, has to be modified just a tad bit to fit - even then, the side marker lights don't line up exactly right -- my next one will be a LeBra even though it leaves a little bit more open in the front, it does seem to fit better (I have seen one on a friend's GT)......... FieroDave - looks good -- here is a pic with the Wolf Bra installed.........<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-523f_01.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||PAUL88GT||05-26-2000||12:49 PM||||Thanks for all the informative feedback. The best price I found on the Colgan bra was $91 plus shipping at Open Road International in Torrence, CA. Does anyone know of a better deal on the Colgan bra? I am leaning toward the Colgan based on the all the comments. Later<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000013||sid1200||05-26-2000||01:56 PM||||I have a factory GM bra on my 88GT although I don't use it much since I don't really like the look<P>however for fit it cant be beat. It goes on via metal hook mounters in the panel screws, as well as velco tape<P>if I am not mistaken the Lebra is the same type of bra and possible was the OEM supplier to GM, I know that it looks the same. covers the area around the side markers<P>quality is good, the bra is 12 years old and feels brand new.<P>WOLF bra, I woulnd't recommened friend has one for his 87 GT, poor fit, materials are not as good, and his bra is only a year old||||reg||1
Z||000014||fropuff||05-26-2000||04:39 PM||||Fierodave, I was still wondering if there is a way to shorten the pieces running up either fender next to the "hood".  Is there?  Thanks||||reg||10
Z||000015||fierodave||05-27-2000||01:13 AM||||fropuff<BR>                 <BR>"Fierodave, I was still wondering if there is a way to shorten the pieces running up either fender next to the "hood". Is there? Thanks"<BR> <BR>I don't know what you want to shorten up!   the part that runs to the fender is a anchor point under the hood for 1 hook and a strip of Velcro™<BR> <BR>I think that's why the Lebra has such a nice fit!<BR>||||reg||1
